        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0772" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg650"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lewis to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 28, 1889</date>.
                        (Received March 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Immediately upon the receipt of Department
                    instructions No. 103, relating to the fine imposed upon the American bark <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Carrie Heckle</hi> by the Portuguese custom-house
                    authorities at Lourenço Marques on the east coast of Africa. I addressed a
                    communication dated 22d instant to Senhor Henrique de Barros Gomes, minister of
                    foreign affairs, a copy of which accompanies this dispatch. I have this day
                    received a communication from Senhor Barros Gomes, and forward inclosed copy and
                    translation thereof.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. P. C. Lewis.</hi></signed></closer>




